--- commit messages
=== 77145ce84353534ba381688d5bbd16ff9ff27aef
KS-1018: type the ks1018 test's JSON bodies and log-call tuples for an including tsc

The project tsc excludes src/__tests__ (KS-1000), so these did not gate;
an including program reported 8 errors in the new file (TS18046 untyped
res.json() bodies, and the logger mock's [object] overload). Casts only;
no runtime change.

Refs KS-1018

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

=== 6e30fe9f5ea3abd8414bfe69db2356d31c2da4d6
KS-1018: the three verification-store reads rethrow infrastructure DB errors as 503 instead of answering from the in-memory map

getVerificationRequest, findPendingVerificationRequest and
listUserVerificationRequests (auth routes/users.ts) caught every DB error with
an empty `catch {}` and answered from the process-local in-memory map, so a DB
outage read as "no such request" (review: 404; list: 200 with no requests;
new request: accepted as if none were pending). Each catch now logs
`DB <fn> failed` with {error, code} and rethrows an infrastructure error as
ServiceUnavailableError (503); any other error falls through as before.

New ks1018-security-correctness-three-verification-store-reads.test.ts: the
READY's two repro cells and control, plus the third site (POST
/me/verification), its non-infra control, and a pin on the log line's meta.

Product lines and the first three cells authored by the local model (Ornith)
from a Wednesday-written brief; source-read by Wednesday; applied, extended
and re-run by seat A.

Refs KS-1018

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

